            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0316" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/5524: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-26T18:00:00+01:00">May 26, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 26—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. The Foreign Office confirmed this morning the reports, circulating locally,
                    that the British Government had communicated with the German Government with
                    regard to the question of the withdrawal of foreign volunteers from Spain, et
                    cetera, and that the German Government favored this idea in principle.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office added that while the German Government was anxious to cooperate in
                    every way for the improvement of conditions <pb facs="0317" n="305"
                        xml:id="pg305"/> in Spain, it felt that the British suggestions were rather
                    vague and that difficult as was the question of the withdrawal of foreign
                    volunteers, the matter should be approached in more concrete and detailed
                    fashion.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office hopes that the deliberations of the Non-intervention Committee
                    in London this week will show progress along this line.</p>
                <p>Copies to London, Paris, Geneva, Rome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
